I0918 16:09:13.161523       1 strace.go:567] [   1:  13] agent-probe E write(0x7 /tmp/summary.txt, 0xf2138b0f680 "RFC 8446 specifies version 1.3 of the Transport Layer Security (TLS) protocol, which provides a secure channel between two communicating peers ensuring authentication, confidentiality, and integrity over a reliable transport. It obsoletes RFCs 5077, 5246, and 6961, and updates RFCs 5705 and 6066, superseding TLS 1.2. TLS 1.3 introduces major changes such as removing legacy and static key-exchange cipher suites in favor of forward-secret (EC)DHE exchanges, encrypting all handshake messages after the ServerHello, and redesigning key derivation using HKDF for improved cryptographic separation. It also adds a 0-RTT mode for faster reconnection (with some security trade-offs), simplifies session resumption via a unified pre-shared key (PSK) mechanism, and streamlines the handshake state machine by removing superfluous messages. The document details the protocol's handshake and record protocols, cryptographic computations, extensions, compliance requirements, and security considerations, including guidance on backw"..., 0x42b)
